# AID Orchestrator — runtime artifacts (not versioned)
# Design artifacts (plans, tasks, config) ARE versioned

# Runtime evidence and execution logs
.aid-o/work/evidence/
.aid-o/work/quick/
.aid-o/work/timeline.jsonl

# Runtime queue state
.aid-o/config/queue.yaml

# Interim brainstorming notes (temporary, deleted after plan completion)
.aid-o/work/interim-*.md

# Legacy v1 structure
.aid-o/04-engine/

# Per-plan execution worktrees (P074) — `plan-start` creates
# .aid-worktrees/plan-<id> as a linked git worktree on plan/<id> and
# plan-close/plan-rollback remove it. Deliberately top-level, NOT under
# .aid-o/: execution trees and AID state stay separated, so tearing a
# worktree down never touches plan state.
.aid-worktrees/

# Runtime state AID writes while it runs: caches, locks, logs, pointers (3.9.1; the list a FSM check
# otherwise saw as "uncommitted changes" — Trading 9. 10. 2026). The plans' own records (plan-state/,
# brainstorm/), backlog.md and aid-plugin-issues.md are NOT here: a project decides to version them.
.aid-o/work/audit-log.jsonl
.aid-o/work/lifecycle-migration.log
.aid-o/work/active.md
.aid-o/work/active.md.pre-index
.aid-o/work/active-runs.json
.aid-o/work/active-run-pointer.json
.aid-o/work/auto-mode-state.yaml
.aid-o/work/codex-probe.json
.aid-o/work/test-durations.jsonl
.aid-o/work/release-force-*
.aid-o/work/companion/
.aid-o/work/superseded-runs/
.aid-o/work/plan-final/
.aid-o/work/runs/
.aid-o/work/test-audits/
.aid-o/work/.cache/
.aid-o/work/*.lock
.aid-o/config/*.lock
.aid-o/.lock
.aid-o/**/*.tmp
.aid-o/metrics/

# UI fidelity runtime outputs (capture sessions, not fixture data)
.aid-o/work/**/ui/

# lib/ui-fidelity node_modules
lib/ui-fidelity/node_modules/
